# Data in Education

A showcase of how data can transform educational decision‑making, pastoral insight, and operational planning.

---
##High School GCSE Tracking and Results Dashboard
  
###Summary of Project
Annual tracking and reviewing of GCSE results in school in the UK has often utilised spreadsheets for review. Analysis tools for results are often exam board specific. Utilising a series of dashboards in Power BI, I created a model to present a whole school executive overview, subject performance with optional filtering by key indicators of gender, SEND, EAL and Pupil Premium, subject comparison and individual student performance for tailored reporting. 

#####Note: 
All student names and data were AI generated from a request for a normally distributed cohort representative of a non-selective school.

###Overview
### Dashboard 1: Overview
![Overview Dashboard](/assets/images/GCSE_overview.png)

A high level overview of key data and demographics. 
Impact scores of results are presented in a series of KPI cards at the top of the page. The main column chart presents distribution of whole school results, while progress through mock series is tracked in the line chart bottom left. The donut charts mid right give year group demographics scatter chart bottom right, while the scatter chart bottom right shows the impact on average GCSE score with attendance, which decreases below the government target of 95% attendance. 
